# Banter in Maidenmist Cemetery (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is maidenmist_cemetery): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ mm_gate_01_rook_tobin
if name:rook_coldwake and name:tobin_hayward and at:mm_gate
interject name:rook_coldwake: That gate's bent outward, Tobin, and the chain's snapped into the mud. Whatever left didn't sign out.
interject name:tobin_hayward: This mud tastes of drowned iron. And that grave by the pickets is sinking straight down.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Poor subsidence control. Decent footing on the fence, though. Mind the soft clay.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Half a verse carved and never finished. Breathe, man. Your chest hasn't moved since the road.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Right. Thank you. I had that scheduled for the gatehouse.
endif
-> END

~ mm_corpse_road_02_delphine_silas
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:silas_vane and at:mm_corpse_road
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Three miles of hearse ruts and not a footlight, Silas. In this fog I'll have to bow by ear.
interject name:silas_vane: Keep off the verge, friend. Every yard of this road is a marked deck of old bones.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: A hearse wheel rotting in the ditch. Your Foolishness is trying to rhyme sepulcher with velour.
interject name:silas_vane: Tell him to fold. The chill past that mile marker is biting my knuckles.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Then walk faster, before the damp takes the starch out of my hem.
endif
-> END

~ mm_gravestones_a_03_lucan_cordelia
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:cordelia_skein and at:mm_gravestones_a
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: These markers are crowded in with no regard for spacing, Cordelia. Barnaby's tail is tucked.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Lovely lichen on this one, though. Oh, look. A stone with its inscription half finished.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, a breach of etiquette. Step wide of that dead tree, if you please. Something's pacing the fog.
interject name:cordelia_skein: I do admire a mason with the nerve to leave a stone half empty.
endif
-> END

~ mm_cremation_gardens_04_silas_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:mm_cremation_gardens
interject name:silas_vane: Ten silver says that wishing fountain is rigged, Lucan. Feel that hum off the tall urn?
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: That's no wager, friend, it's a resonance. A mournful one. Barnaby is staring at those purple coals.
interject name:silas_vane: Half these urns are dead quiet and the other half won't shut up.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The lavender masks the wet ash nicely. And a gentleman doesn't shake the urns to see who's inside.
interject name:silas_vane: Wasn't gonna shake 'em, friend. Just reading the fine print on the plaque.
endif
-> END

~ mm_mausoleum_lanes_05_cordelia_silas
if name:cordelia_skein and name:silas_vane and at:mm_mausoleum_lanes
interject name:cordelia_skein: Mind the cracks, Silas. Every vault here has a spiral or a ship on it. A catalogue of drownings.
interject name:silas_vane: Takes me back to the river landings. Except here the landlords lock the doors from outside.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Those pink coals by the mossy tree. The air off this lane is remarkably acrid.
interject name:silas_vane: Nobody carves a ship on a stone box unless they expect the tide to come up.
endif
-> END

~ mm_kings_rest_06_delphine_lucan
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:mm_kings_rest
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Now that's billing, Lucan. A stone king raising his blade through the fog.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Eight out of ten for scale. But those guards at his doors have traded the same lunge for an age.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Broken iron everywhere, and none of them looks at the house. Why put on a show and never bow?
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Because what they guard is long cold behind those doors. Even a hound lies down when the master's gone.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Well, keep Barnaby at heel. I've no wish to mend a spectral collar tonight.
endif
-> END

~ mm_shadestone_sanctuary_07_silas_rook
if name:silas_vane and name:rook_coldwake and at:mm_shadestone_sanctuary
interject name:silas_vane: Air's clean here, Rook. That blue fire burns steady as a lighthouse. And a shovel laid across the slab.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Tools down, shift ended, proper and square. Whoever cut these orc names left a tidy record.
interject name:silas_vane: Makes a bloke want to check the tallies in his own ribs.
interject name:rook_coldwake: A monument isn't a tab to collect, Silas. You leave the ledger as it lies, and keep watch.
interject name:silas_vane: Fair enough. Strange, a lantern statue that doesn't make my bones itch.
endif
-> END

~ mm_necropolis_depths_08_rook_cordelia
if name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:mm_necropolis_depths and not flag.necrolisk_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Grey mist leaking through the cracks, and something clawed this burrow with no thought for the stone.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Look how the slime preserves things in the wall, Rook. My eyes are clicking so loud I can't hear the drips.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Keep your vials clear of it. That smell is old meat and bad drainage.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Don't fret, darling. Let's clear the cavern before it ruins my waistcoat.
endif
-> END
